      "problem": "In the regular heptagon $ABCDEFG$, we have $CD=2\\,cm.$ What is the perimeter of the heptagon?",
      "worked_solution": "The perimeter $p$ of a polygon is the sum of the measures of all its sides. Since all the sides of a regular heptagon are equal and the measure of one of them is $2\\,cm$, we have \n\n$$\np=7\\cdot CD=7\\cdot 2=14\\,cm.\n$$",
